meta {
  name: List Leads
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/leads?page=1&pageSize=50
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  pageSize: 50
  ~search: rodriguez
  ~status: New,Requote
  ~temperature: Hot,Warm
  ~leadSource: Mailer
  ~producerId: {{producerId}}
  ~householdId: {{householdId}}
  ~dateFrom: 2026-01-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-12-31
  ~scope: own
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

script:post-response {
  // Capture the first row's id for the Lead Detail requests (PAC-38).
  // Runtime-only var (never persisted to disk).
  if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    if (items && items.length > 0) {
      bru.setVar("leadId", items[0].id);
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns a paginated envelope", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("page");
    expect(body).to.have.property("pageSize");
    expect(body).to.have.property("total");
    expect(body).to.have.property("totalPages");
    expect(body).to.have.property("items");
    expect(body.items).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("rows expose only display fields (no internals leak)", function () {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    if (items.length > 0) {
      const row = items[0];
      expect(row).to.have.property("name");
      expect(row).to.have.property("status");
      expect(row).to.have.property("temperature");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("legacySmartSuiteId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("legacyProducerId");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("isTestRecord");
      expect(row).to.not.have.property("agencyId");
    }
  });

  test("status is a normalized label, never a raw SmartSuite code", function () {
    const items = res.getBody().items;
    const rawCodes = ["arW7O", "phjnb", "jp76g", "hfwda"];
    items.forEach(function (row) {
      expect(rawCodes).to.not.include(row.status);
    });
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /leads — Leads list (PAC-36)

  The read path behind the `/leads` page: the caller's leads, filtered and
  searched **entirely server-side** and sorted by last activity (newest first).

  Because nothing is post-filtered in memory, `total` and the page arithmetic
  are exact for every filter/search combination — a deliberate behaviour change
  from the legacy SmartSuite-backed endpoint, whose totals were window-local.

  - **Module:** `leads` (must be enabled for the agency)
  - **Permission:** `leads:read`
  - **Data scope** (enforced in the service layer, never the controller):
    - `own` → only the caller's own leads (`producerId = user`). A
      `scope=agency` or foreign `producerId` in the query is **silently
      ignored** — it never errors and never widens the result set.
    - `branch` → leads in the caller's branch (or the `X-Branch-Id` branch);
      a supplied `producerId` narrows *within* the branch.
    - `agency` → all leads in the agency.
  - Records flagged `isTestRecord` are always excluded.

  ## Query params
  | param       | type    | default | rules                                             |
  |-------------|---------|---------|---------------------------------------------------|
  | page        | int     | 1       | min 1 (1-based)                                   |
  | pageSize    | int     | 50      | min 1, max 100                                    |
  | search      | string  | —       | max 120 chars; interpreted by shape (see below)   |
  | status      | multi   | —       | canonical labels, e.g. `New`, `Requote`; max 10   |
  | temperature | multi   | —       | `Hot` \| `Warm` \| `Cold` \| `Unknown`; max 4     |
  | leadSource  | string  | —       | canonical label, e.g. `Mailer`                    |
  | producerId  | string  | —       | ObjectId; ignored for `own` scope                 |
  | householdId | string  | —       | ObjectId (24 hex); narrows to one household       |
  | dateFrom    | date    | —       | filters `createdDate` (inclusive)                 |
  | dateTo      | date    | —       | filters `createdDate` (inclusive, whole day)      |
  | scope       | enum    | —       | `own` \| `agency`; clamped to the caller's scope  |

  ### Multi-value params (`status`, `temperature`)
  Both are **multi-select** — several values are ORed together. Three request
  forms are accepted and normalized identically (trimmed + deduped):

  - repeated: `?status=New&status=Requote`
  - comma-separated: `?status=New,Requote`
  - single: `?status=New`

  An empty or whitespace-only value is treated as *no filter*, not as an
  impossible one — clearing the UI filter never returns an empty list. Each
  element of `temperature` must be a valid enum member; one bad value rejects
  the whole request (`400`).

  ### `householdId`
  Every lead attached to one household — the lead picker in the Household
  page's "Start Quote" dialog, which offers the household's existing leads
  before offering to create one.

  It narrows *within* the data-scope clamp and never widens it: a producer
  (`own`) still sees only their own leads for that household, so a colleague's
  lead on the same household is simply absent rather than forbidden. A value
  that is not 24 hex characters is a `400`, not a `500` — the shape is checked
  in the DTO so a malformed id never reaches Mongoose as a `CastError`.

  ### How `search` is interpreted
  One branch is chosen by the shape of the query:

  1. contains `@` → **email** match across the `emails` array
  2. else ≥ 7 digits after stripping non-digits → **phone** (digit-tolerant, so
     `5551234` matches `(555) 123-4xxx`) **or** quote control number
  3. else → **name** (first, last, or the combined `first last`), **lead source
     label**, or **quote control number**

  Note `status` accepts canonical labels and matches migrated documents that
  store the raw SmartSuite code — filtering `Requote` also finds `arW7O`. Each
  selected label expands to its own code set before the values are ORed.

  ## Headers
  - `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>` — inherited from the collection.
  - `X-Branch-Id` *(optional)* — disabled by default. Only relevant for
    `branch`/`agency` callers targeting a specific branch; ignored for
    producers (`own` scope).

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "page": 1,
    "pageSize": 50,
    "total": 40,
    "totalPages": 1,
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "665f...ac1",
        "name": "Maria Rodriguez",
        "leadSource": "Mailer",
        "status": "New",
        "temperature": "Hot",
        "phone": "5551234567",
        "email": "maria.rodriguez@example.com",
        "updatedAt": "2026-07-28T14:02:11.000Z"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  Row fields:
  | field       | type           | notes                                                    |
  |-------------|----------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
  | id          | string         | record id — the only identifier exposed                  |
  | name        | string         | `first last`, or `"Unknown Lead"` when both are empty    |
  | leadSource  | string         | normalized label, never a raw choice code                |
  | status      | string         | canonical label — `arW7O` is normalized to `Requote`     |
  | temperature | enum           | `Hot` \| `Warm` \| `Cold` \| `Unknown`                   |
  | phone       | string \| null | first phone as stored; the client formats it             |
  | email       | string \| null | first email                                              |
  | updatedAt   | string \| null | ISO last-activity timestamp; drives the default sort     |

  No `legacy*` ids, `isTestRecord`, `agencyId`/`branchId`, or raw documents are
  ever returned.

  ## Errors
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `leads` module disabled, or missing `leads:read`.
  - `400 Bad Request` — invalid query params (e.g. `pageSize` > 100, `page` < 1,
    an unknown `temperature`, more than 10 `status` values, an unparseable
    `dateFrom`/`dateTo`, a `householdId` that is not a record id).

  > **Tip:** the seeded producer (`producer@demoagency.local`) is the
  > data-rich user for this list. Log in as them to get non-empty results.
}
